\documentclass{article}
\title{A Daily Pipeline for Ferry Timetable Publishing}
\author{K. Saarinen and P. Novak}
\date{March 2026}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Data Flow}
Every morning the export job pulls the day's timetable from the scheduling database.
It first validates route_code against the published register
and then refreshes berth_no so the departure boards always show the latest assignment.
Crossings that fail validation are held back for manual review,
and the held queue is summarised in the midday bulletin.

\section{Publishing}
Once the checks pass, the timetable is pushed to the booking API
and to the displays at each terminal.
A copy is archived with the date stamped in the file header.
\end{document}

